# Detector-systematic importance scan against a single cache.
#
#   scripts/submit_fanout.sh --queue capacity --walltime 03:00:00 \
#       --variants jobs/contours/scan_detsyst.variants \
#       jobs/contours/contours_full.ini -- surface -g 30 --xlo 1e-2 --ylo 1e-1
#
# Each line becomes one rank: the base config with those systematics removed
# via --exclude-systs. All ranks share contours_full's tag and therefore its
# cache, so the whole scan costs one fit's wall-clock and no processing -
# --exclude-systs is applied at load time, not at process time.
#
# 10 variants = 10 nodes, within capacity's 16-node ceiling.
#
# FORMAT: whitespace-separated.
#   label     becomes -o <label> and <label>.log, so it must be unique and
#             contain no spaces
#   exclude   one or more names passed to --exclude-systs
#
# ICARUS ENTRIES DROP BOTH RUNS. Every ICARUS detector systematic exists as a
# separate _icarus_Run2 and _icarus_Run4 entry, but they are one physical
# effect. Removing only one run leaves the other constraining the fit and
# answers nothing, so each ICARUS line lists both.
#
# USE THE XML `name=`, NOT THE TAG OR PLOTNAME. --exclude-systs resolves a tag
# first, so `Detector Systematics` would drop all 12 detector systematics rather
# than one. Plotnames like "WireMod yz SBND" contain spaces and would be split
# into separate arguments.
#
# WATCH THE BASE NAMES - THEY ARE NOT SYMMETRIC. SBND's charge-scale entry is
# `ChargeScale15_sbnd_Run1` while ICARUS's are `ChargeScale_icarus_Run*`, and
# DENT exists only for SBND while SCE exists only for ICARUS. Check against the
# XML rather than assuming a naming pattern.
#
# SILENT FAILURE: a name matching nothing excludes nothing, and the run still
# produces a perfectly plausible contour identical to the baseline. Verify each
# variant dropped the expected number of fitted systematic parameters rather
# than trusting the label. The `Excluding systematic X by command line
# argument` log line only proves the argument was passed, not that it matched.
#
# Excluded from this scan: ToroidCalibration and ProtonMiss, which are tagged
# POT Normalization rather than Detector Systematics.
#
# label            exclude
# --- SBND ---
nowmyz             WireModYZ_sbnd_Run1
nowmxtxw           WireModxThetaXW_sbnd_Run1
nochargescale      ChargeScale15_sbnd_Run1
nodent             DENT_sbnd_Run1
notrigemu          TriggerEmulation_sbnd_Run1
# --- ICARUS (both runs per line) ---
noicwmyz           WireModYZ_icarus_Run2        WireModYZ_icarus_Run4
noicwmxtxw         WireModxThetaXW_icarus_Run2  WireModxThetaXW_icarus_Run4
noicchargescale    ChargeScale_icarus_Run2      ChargeScale_icarus_Run4
noicsce            SCE_icarus_Run2              SCE_icarus_Run4
noictrigemu        TriggerEmulation_icarus_Run2 TriggerEmulation_icarus_Run4
